###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Fitting parameters of all models are in the Supporting Information, which is not part of the PDF read; no hyperparameter setting, loss or software is encoded.
# - The retrained ANI models start from the ANI-2x weights (stated by the authors as a considerable advantage); schema 0.1.2 cannot link them to the registry model ANI-2x, so this is in the run labels only.
# - The reference level of rMD17 is not restated in the paper, so the rMD17 data sets carry no reference calculation.
# - Not encoded: the FCHL column (not trained by the authors), the literature columns of Tables 2 and 3 (PaiNN, GMsNN, DimeNet and others, trained on the original MD17), the reparametrised classical force field (not an MLIP), the combined-fit Table 4, and the extrapolation tests beyond RMSE (normal modes, dihedral scans, high-temperature stability), which are figures or have no MetricProperty.
# - For the ANI-2x rows of Table 6 the two blocks (fit to 300 K, fit to mixed-T) repeat the same values, since ANI-2x is not refitted; they are encoded once.
# - Which potential drove the 25 ps sampling MD of 3BPA is not stated in the parts read.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
